1
00:00:01,730 --> 00:00:26,060
Autonomy and execution
A goal in plain English. The real model chooses actions; Chromium performs the work.

2
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:34,910
Verification: saved row and browser evidence
The persisted record matches the source: X-101, USD 1,240.50, due 2026-10-31.

3
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:54,920
Generalization: a read-only task
A different vendor and objective use the same engine. Reporting makes no ledger write.

4
00:00:54,920 --> 00:01:16,440
Generalization: multiple documents
The same worker records all Company X invoices instead of only the latest one.

5
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:43,880
Product thinking: approval before a high-value write
Northstar's USD 7,800 record requires a human decision. The worker pauses before writing.

6
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:58,812
Product thinking: ask instead of guessing
A missing source due date stops the task. The worker does not invent a value.
